15. Welcomes the proposed actions powering the circular economy and the bioeconomy by securing access to materials and resources; encourages the Circular Economy Act to include strategies for chemical raw materials to safeguard detoxified material cycles, especially in solutions free of per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFAS), and measures to increase the use and affordability of strategic secondary materials within the EU taking into consideration the aims of the Critical Raw Materials Act11; stresses the need to define those secondary raw materials that are strategic and that should be subject to export monitoring, such as steel and metal scrap, and to tackle any imbalance in their supply and demand, including by exploring export restrictions; insists on the effective enforcement of the Waste Shipment Regulation12; calls for a predictable regulatory framework that unlocks circular business models, particularly those based on waste prevention, reuse, high-quality recycling; stresses that communities living near pollution hotspots, such as areas affected by PFAS, deserve justice through comprehensive measures including pollution prevention, monitoring, soil sanitation, health initiatives and tailored response plans to address their needs; stresses that polluting companies must be held accountable for covering the costs of pollution prevention at its source and providing compensation, and that the ‘polluter pays’ principle should be enforced, requiring companies to contribute to independently managed funds focused on depollution efforts; stresses that this strategy must ensure policy coherence with the upcoming REACH Directive12a and the Water Framework Directive12b;

---

11 Regulation (EU) 2024/1252 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 April 2024 establishing a framework for ensuring a secure and sustainable supply of critical raw materials and amending Regulations (EU) No 168/2013, (EU) 2018/858, (EU) 2018/1724 and (EU) 2019/1020 (OJ L, 2024/1252, 3.5.2024, ELI: ). 12 Regulation (EU) 2024/1157 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 April 2024 on shipments of waste, amending Regulations (EU) No 1257/2013 and (EU) 2020/1056 and repealing Regulation (EC) No 1013/2006 (OJ L, 2024/1157, 30.4.2024, ELI: ). 12a Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 18 December 2006 concerning the Registration, Evaluation, Authorisation and Restriction of Chemicals (REACH), establishing a European Chemicals Agency, amending Directive 1999/45/EC and repealing Council Regulation (EEC) No 793/93 and Commission Regulation (EC) No 1488/94 as well as Council Directive 76/769/EEC and Commission Directives 91/155/EEC, 93/67/EEC, 93/105/EC and 2000/21/EC (*OJ L 396, 30.12.2006, p. 1, *ELI:[http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2006/1907/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2006/1907/oj)). 12b Directive 2000/60/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 October 2000 establishing a framework for Community action in the field of water policy (*OJ L 327, 22.12.2000, p. 1, *ELI:[http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/60/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2000/60/oj)).
